1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,312
A Table by the Window.

3
00:00:03,312 --> 00:00:06,583
Mom, Ben, and I stop at a diner for lunch.

4
00:00:06,583 --> 00:00:09,948
I spot a table by the window with sunlight falling across it.

5
00:00:09,948 --> 00:00:14,010
Unfortunately, another family spots it about three seconds before I do.

6
00:00:14,284 --> 00:00:16,515
A table for three, please.

7
00:00:16,756 --> 00:00:18,052
Of course.

8
00:00:18,052 --> 00:00:20,354
We have a booth available near the back.

9
00:00:20,644 --> 00:00:22,728
Could we sit by the window instead?

10
00:00:22,948 --> 00:00:26,002
You can, but those tables are all taken right now.

11
00:00:26,236 --> 00:00:27,873
How long is the wait?

12
00:00:28,108 --> 00:00:30,445
Probably fifteen or twenty minutes.

13
00:00:30,445 --> 00:00:32,654
I can't promise an exact time.

14
00:00:32,932 --> 00:00:35,674
My stomach says that is a very long time.

15
00:00:35,908 --> 00:00:37,964
I look at the booth near the back.

16
00:00:37,964 --> 00:00:41,943
It has soft seats and a tiny picture of a dog wearing sunglasses above it.

17
00:00:41,943 --> 00:00:44,308
Actually, this table is fine.

18
00:00:44,572 --> 00:00:46,003
Right this way.

19
00:00:46,003 --> 00:00:47,743
Here are your menus.

20
00:00:47,743 --> 00:00:49,587
I'll give you a few minutes.

21
00:00:49,852 --> 00:00:51,648
We slide into the booth.

22
00:00:51,648 --> 00:00:55,700
Ben immediately points at the dog picture and decides it's the owner of the restaurant.

23
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:57,820
A dog who runs a diner?

24
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,497
That's a busy dog.

25
00:00:59,764 --> 00:01:02,651
He probably checks all the hamburgers personally.

26
00:01:02,884 --> 00:01:05,690
We order lunch and share a glass bottle of ketchup.

27
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:09,659
By the time our food arrives, I have completely forgotten about the window.

28
00:01:09,659 --> 00:01:14,169
The booth is comfortable, Ben is telling dog stories, and Mom looks relaxed.

29
00:01:14,452 --> 00:01:16,296
Still wish we had waited?

30
00:01:16,516 --> 00:01:17,801
Not at all.

31
00:01:17,801 --> 00:01:19,989
This table comes with entertainment.

32
00:01:19,989 --> 00:01:21,520
I point to Ben.

33
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:24,645
Unfortunately, there doesn't seem to be an off switch.
